      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can confirm this bug. The Quest OS is fighting me every step of the way trying to get the client log file, but this should be very easy for VRChat to replicate.\n\nCreate a new meta account, add it to the headset, install vrchat, launch, try to load a youtube link. Fails instantly. \n\nNote that videos which do not rely on direct link resolution through ytdlp work fine. Looking at my server logs, when using a secondary account I do not see ytdlp making any requests for this content. The requests instead come from the video player useragent only, so perhaps ytdlp is not running at all and the original URL is falling through to the player.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
